+# August 24 messages add a specific intelligence-link request, not the missing final decision
+
+October 29, 2026, America/New_York. **Newly acquired court exhibits 636 and 637 document Samit's report of a possible CIA/CTC-supplied connection and his request to establish a firmer connection for the search-warrant argument.** They preserve a contemporaneous difference between the field investigator's assessment and the headquarters position he reports. They do not supply the underlying intelligence, native attachments, an attorney's original advice, an issued warrant or the final search decision.
+
+## 636: an anticipated handoff and a possible connection
+
+[Exhibit 636](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/636.pdf), physical page 1, is a displayed Samit message dated **8/24/01**, subject **Pending Matter - UBL Connections**. Its first body paragraph says the case moved from the Iran Unit to RFU and appeared headed toward the recipients because of possible UBL connections. This is Samit's account of the case's route and anticipated next destination, not an authenticated routing log or acknowledgment that a particular office received the package.
+
+The **second body paragraph** refers the reader to background or an attachment and attributes a possible UBL connection to the Agency/CTC, based on French information and the claimed Ibn Khatab association. The source's qualifier is important: **possible**, not a demonstrated operational link. The underlying French information and CIA assessment are not attached as native files to this single-page court copy. No masked source or recipient identity is reconstructed.
+
+The **closing body paragraph** expresses hope that the matter will reach the recipients. It does not certify that the handoff occurred. Read the attachment reference as a concrete retrieval target, not proof that the court PDF contains it or that every later reviewer saw it.
+
+## 637: the requested link and the competing assessment are on the same page
+
+[Exhibit 637](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/637.pdf), physical page 1, is a displayed Samit message dated **8/24/01 2:16PM**, subject **Short Notice Request**. Its header includes a redacted recipient field and a visible Jones recipient. A salutation is not an authenticated identification of the masked recipient, and this review does not infer an agency affiliation behind that field.
+
+Counting the narrative paragraphs after the salutation:
+
+1. **Paragraph 1** says an opening EC and Legat Paris information are attached. Those are specifically named missing counterparts, rather than proof of an authenticated complete delivery.
+2. **Paragraph 3** describes the laptop, manuals and notebooks, says a criminal or FISC-authorized warrant is needed to search, and warns of a **one-week** interval before possible UK deportation with the property. These are the investigator's account and anticipated risk; no completed deportation, property release, deletion or search is demonstrated here.
+3. **Paragraph 4** attributes to FBIHQ/CTD/ITOS/RFU insufficient criminal evidence and an insufficient foreign-power connection because the named-group relationship had not been established. Samit expressly disagrees. This is a contemporaneous participant's report of headquarters' position, not headquarters' own legal opinion or this report's statement of the governing legal test.
+4. **Paragraph 5** attributes assistance to CIA/CTC concerning the claimed Ibn Khatab–UBL association, but says a definitive UBL/Al-Qaeda connection is still sought to supply the named group. Substantial adjacent text remains redacted. The visible conditional request and the reported assistance must remain together; neither turns the other into proof of affiliation or a fully established legal basis.
+
+Paragraph 2's biographical information, the contact details in the other exhibit and scan signatures are unnecessary to this finding and are not reproduced in the public notes. No concealed request is filled in from surrounding text.
+
+## Compare the records without blending them into a single answer
+
+| Source and exact locator | Observation to preserve | Qualification or conflicting account to preserve |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| **348 p1, second body paragraph and closing request**, displayed August 24 | Samit reports a provisional criminal/foreign-power obstacle and asks for British information. | His seeming/thus-far framing and explicit disagreement are not an acquired legal-unit decision. The conditional UK scenario is not an executed alternative. |
+| **636 p1, first two body paragraphs**, displayed August 24 | Samit anticipates a further route and attributes a possible UBL connection to Agency/CTC and French information. | Possible is not definitive; anticipation is not receipt. The actual attached background/intelligence is missing. |
+| **637 p1, paragraphs 3–5**, displayed August 24 | Samit reports the obstacle, CIA assistance and the need for a firmer link while seeking search authority. | These are the same author's accounts, not independent agency confirmation. The message does not demonstrate which evidentiary package headquarters or counsel received. |
+| **349 p1, item 1 and quoted message at bottom**, displayed August 28 | Jones questions proposed later addition of the foreign-power material and warns about the initial review's prospects. | The August 24 accounts do not authenticate the missing draft attachment or prove what was included in that particular initial-review package. |
+| **350 p1, item 1**, displayed August 28 | Maltbie says foreign-power material is being assembled and will be added if the package reaches a possible OIPR stage. | His sequence/explanation remains beside the earlier possible-link reporting and Jones's objection. This is not proof of actual OIPR referral, deliberate omission or a completed legal disposition. |
+| **351 p1, first quoted body paragraph and following paragraph**, displayed August 28 | Maltbie reports a Bowman/NSLU meeting and insufficient foreign-power connection, then proposes further work with LEGAT assistance. | Bowman’s own advice and actual meeting inputs remain missing. Proposed further work is contrary evidence to a blanket account that every investigative effort stopped; execution and adequacy still require records. |
+
+The new messages make the question more precise: **what underlying information existed, how strongly did it support each asserted link, which version and attachments reached each reviewer, and what was decided on those inputs?** They supply documentary support for investigating that chain. They do not establish that the chain was deliberately interrupted or that a warrant should necessarily have issued.
+
+The possible-connection wording in 636 and the definitive-connection request in 637 are preserved as different confidence/threshold formulations. They are not silently reconciled, or labeled two logically incompatible completed findings. Similarly, the earlier awareness of an alleged association and a later proposal to assemble or add a foreign-power argument are different propositions. The records leave a package/version/knowledge question; the cause of that difference is not adjudicated.
+
+The previously preserved **693 August 24 face date versus August 28 addition discussion**, and **693/347 visible text versus redactions**, remain in the [349/693 review](../moussaoui-349-693-comparison-2026-10-29/README.md). Neither LHM is newly reread here or authenticated as the missing August 28 attachment. No redacted paragraph is treated as absent or reconstructed. Header times lack native timezone/transport authentication; no elapsed-time calculation or minute-by-minute historical sequence is asserted.
+
+## What this supports, and what could weaken it
+
+**Directly observed:** the two court-copy messages contain an attributed CIA/CTC assistance claim, a possible-link assessment, a request for a firmer link, a reported HQ disagreement and explicit attachment references. This is narrower than independently proving the underlying intelligence or its receipt.
+
+**Reasonable lead:** compare the French/CIA source materials and recipient copies against the actual draft versions and legal advice. If a reviewer possessed stronger relevant material that was knowingly omitted or misrepresented, contemporaneous inputs and instructions could support that interpretation. If the material was tentative, did not establish the asserted chain, was included elsewhere, or was assessed under a different legally relevant question, those records could weaken it. None of those possibilities is selected as the explanation here.
+
+**Contrary evidence and dependence:** 636/637 and 348 repeat one investigator's accounts; they are not three independent confirmations. These messages show active efforts to obtain information and search authority. Maltbie's accuracy/sequencing rationale and reported legal review remain preserved, rather than discarded because they differ from the field account. Neither suspicion nor an innocent explanation substitutes for the missing originals.
+
+## TODOs retained; scope actually completed
+
+[OPEN-TODOS.json](OPEN-TODOS.json) retains **DRAFT-T01–T06**. The exact next inputs are the attached opening EC, Paris information/background, original CIA/CTC association assessment and recipient task/reply, the actual draft/package versions, Bowman's original advice and any referral/nonreferral/order/return. A filename or exhibit title alone does not identify one of those counterparts. The court's separately linked **326 response**, **639 update** and **336/337 French-information copies** are concrete candidate controls, not acquired/read results of this unit.
+
+All eighteen original-input requirements in the five-track plan remain open: these messages do not replace FAA correction/receipt or signed disposition records, native telephone joins, recorder/clock authentication, specimen/instrument measurements or steel-custody/attribution records. No goal-completion claim follows from publication.
+
+**Actual reading:** both new single-page PDFs were read visually in full at 160 dpi. The complete single pages of 348, 349, 350 and 351 were reinspected from held renders. The other sources are attributed to the preserved prior studies, not claimed newly read. Both new PDFs yielded zero extracted text characters and no passively exposed embedded attachment names. No OCR, native-message reconstruction, signature/handwriting authentication, original intelligence validation, legal adjudication, physical test or historical cause/intent finding was performed.
+
+Original source bytes, redactions, page order and earlier reports remain unchanged. [SOURCES.json](SOURCES.json) records URLs, access times, bytes and SHA-256; [OBSERVATIONS.json](OBSERVATIONS.json) pins statements to PDF paragraphs and this report's line numbers. [SOURCE-CHECKS.json](SOURCE-CHECKS.json) records integrity/structure checks, not independent validation of visual readings or historical truth. [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff) is the exact research-note addition, not a native-message or draft-version diff. Public additions exclude raw scans/rasters/OCR, personal/contact/account details, signatures, private correspondence and strategy. No outreach, fee, new request/filing, mailbox access, deletion, private push, merge or history rewrite occurred.
